/-!
# Additive polynomials

A polynomial `f` over a commutative ring `R` is *additive* when `f(X + Y) = f(X) + f(Y)` in the
bivariate polynomial ring `R[X][Y]`; it then satisfies `f(x + y) = f(x) + f(y)` in every commutative
`R`-algebra. Comparing the coefficients of `X ^ a * Y ^ b`, which are `(a + b).choose a • f_{a+b}`
on the left, `f` is additive exactly when its constant coefficient vanishes and
`(a + b).choose a • f_{a+b} = 0` for all positive `a` and `b`. This is the coefficient criterion
`PowerSeries.subst_add_eq_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_and_choose_mul_coeff_eq_zero` for `f` viewed
as a power series. In prime characteristic `p` every middle binomial coefficient of `n` vanishes
exactly when `n` is a power of `p` (Lucas, via `PowerSeries.subst_add_eq_iff_coeff_eq_zero`), so
the additive polynomials are the *`p`-polynomials*, the `R`-linear combinations of the `X ^ p ^ i`
(Goss, Chapter 1). These are the endomorphisms of the additive group in characteristic
`p`.

The rest of the file is about the additive polynomial of a finite additive subgroup.

For a finite additive subgroup `V` of a commutative ring `R`, the monic polynomial

`a_V = ∏_{c ∈ V} (X - c)`

is Lagrange's `nodal` polynomial at the nodes `V`; it has degree `|V|`. Since `V` is a subgroup,
translating by an element of `V` permutes the factors, so `a_V (x + c) = a_V x` for `c ∈ V`.

Over a domain `R`, evaluation of `a_V` in any commutative `R`-algebra `A` is additive:

`a_V (x + y) = a_V x + a_V y`.

In a domain, the polynomial `a_V (X + y) - a_V X - a_V y` has degree less than `|V|`, since both
`a_V (X + y)` and `a_V X` are monic of degree `|V|`, and it vanishes at the `|V|` distinct points
of `V`. This gives an identity in a polynomial domain, which evaluates to the identity in any
commutative `R`-algebra. The domain hypothesis cannot be dropped: for `V = {0, 2}` in `ℤ/4ℤ`,
`a_V = X ^ 2 - 2 * X` and `a_V (x + y) - a_V x - a_V y = 2 * x * y`. No characteristic hypothesis
is needed; in characteristic zero the only finite additive subgroup of a domain is `0`. In
characteristic `p`, a monic separable additive polynomial all of whose roots lie in a field `K` is
`a_V` for its group of roots `V`. Over a domain the derivative of `a_V` is the constant
`∏_{c ∈ V, c ≠ 0} (-c)`, which is a unit over a field, so there `a_V - u` is separable.

The equations `a_V (y) = u` define the elementary abelian Artin–Schreier extensions: an extension
generated by such a `y` is Galois with group isomorphic to a subgroup of `V`, and to `V` itself
when its degree is `|V|` (Stichtenoth, Proposition 3.7.10). For `V` the prime field of a field of
characteristic `p`, `a_V = X ^ p - X`.

## Main definitions

* `AddSubgroup.additivePolynomial`: the polynomial `∏_{c ∈ V} (X - c)`.

## Main results

* `Polynomial.aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq_iff`: `f(X + Y) = f(X) + f(Y)` exactly when `f_0 = 0` and
  `(a + b).choose a * f_{a+b} = 0` for all positive `a`, `b`.
* `Polynomial.aeval_add_of_aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq`: an additive polynomial is additive in every
  commutative algebra.
* `Polynomial.aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq_iff_mem_span`: in prime characteristic `p`, the additive
  polynomials are the `R`-linear combinations of the `X ^ p ^ i`.
* `AddSubgroup.aeval_additivePolynomial_add_algebraMap`: `a_V (x + c) = a_V x` for `c ∈ V`.
* `AddSubgroup.aeval_additivePolynomial_eq_zero_iff`: the roots of `a_V` in an `R`-algebra
  without zero divisors are the images under `algebraMap R A` of the elements of `V`.
* `AddSubgroup.aeval_additivePolynomial_add`: `a_V (x + y) = a_V x + a_V y`.
* `AddSubgroup.map_additivePolynomial_sub_C_eq_prod`: `a_V - u = ∏_{c ∈ V} (X - (y + c))`.
* `AddSubgroup.splits_additivePolynomial_sub_C`: `a_V - u` splits in any commutative `R`-algebra
  containing one of its roots.
* `AddSubgroup.derivative_additivePolynomial`: the derivative of `a_V` is the constant
  `∏_{c ∈ V, c ≠ 0} (-c)`.
* `AddSubgroup.isIntegral_of_aeval_additivePolynomial_eq`: a root of `a_V - u` is integral.
* `AddSubgroup.separable_additivePolynomial`: over a field, `a_V` is separable.
* `AddSubgroup.separable_additivePolynomial_sub_C`: over a field, `a_V - u` is separable.

## References

* H. Stichtenoth, *Algebraic Function Fields and Codes*, 2nd ed., GTM 254, Springer, 2009,
  Proposition 3.7.10.
* D. Goss, *Basic Structures of Function Field Arithmetic*, Springer, 1996, Chapter 1
  (additive polynomials).
-/

public section

open Polynomial

namespace Polynomial

open Bivariate

section CommSemiring

variable {R : Type*} [CommSemiring R]

/-- A polynomial satisfying `f(X + Y) = f(X) + f(Y)` is additive in every commutative algebra. -/
theorem aeval_add_of_aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq {A : Type*} [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A] {f : R[X]}
    (hf : aeval (C X + Y : R[X][Y]) f = C f + f.map C) (x y : A) :
    aeval (x + y) f = aeval x f + aeval y f := by
  have hmap : f.map C = aeval (Y : R[X][Y]) f := (aeval_X_left_eq_map f).symm
  have h := congrArg (aevalAeval x y) hf
  rwa [hmap, ← aeval_algHom_apply, map_add, aevalAeval_X, aevalAeval_Y, map_add, aevalAeval_C,
    ← aeval_algHom_apply, aevalAeval_Y] at h

/-- A polynomial satisfies `f(X + Y) = f(X) + f(Y)` exactly when its constant coefficient vanishes
and `(a + b).choose a * f_{a+b} = 0` for all positive `a` and `b`. -/
theorem aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq_iff [IsCancelAdd R] {f : R[X]} :
    aeval (C X + Y : R[X][Y]) f = C f + f.map C ↔
      f.coeff 0 = 0 ∧ ∀ a b, a ≠ 0 → b ≠ 0 → ((a + b).choose a : R) * f.coeff (a + b) = 0 := by
  simp only [AddMonoidAlgebra.ext_iff, DFunLike.ext_iff, coeff_coeff_aeval_C_X_add_Y, coeff_add,
    coeff_C, coeff_map]
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine ⟨by simpa using h 0 0, fun a b ha hb => ?_⟩
    rw [Nat.choose_symm_add]
    simpa [ha, hb] using h b a
  · rintro ⟨h0, h⟩ b a
    rcases eq_or_ne a 0 with rfl | ha <;> rcases eq_or_ne b 0 with rfl | hb
    · simp [h0]
    · simp [hb]
    · simp [ha]
    · rw [← Nat.choose_symm_add]
      simpa [ha, hb] using h a b ha hb

end CommSemiring

section CommRing

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- Over a ring killed by a prime `p`, a polynomial satisfies `f(X + Y) = f(X) + f(Y)` exactly
when it is a `p`-polynomial: an `R`-linear combination of the powers `X ^ p ^ i`. -/
theorem aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq_iff_mem_span (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hR : (p : R) = 0) {f : R[X]} :
    aeval (C X + Y : R[X][Y]) f = C f + f.map C ↔
      f ∈ Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i => (X : R[X]) ^ p ^ i) := by
  have hspan : Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i => (X : R[X]) ^ p ^ i) =
      AddMonoidAlgebra.supported R R (Set.range (p ^ ·)) := by
    rw [AddMonoidAlgebra.supported_eq_span_single, ← Set.range_comp]
    simp [Function.comp_def, single_eq_monomial, X_pow_eq_monomial]
  -- The coefficient criterion is the one for `f` as a power series, whose prime-characteristic
  -- form is the support criterion `PowerSeries.subst_add_eq_iff_coeff_eq_zero`.
  have hseries := (PowerSeries.subst_add_eq_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_and_choose_mul_coeff_eq_zero
    (f : PowerSeries R)).symm.trans <|
      PowerSeries.subst_add_eq_iff_coeff_eq_zero (f : PowerSeries R) (Fact.out : p.Prime) hR
  simp only [coeff_coe, constantCoeff_coe, Nat.pos_iff_ne_zero] at hseries
  rw [aeval_C_X_add_Y_eq_iff, hseries, hspan, AddMonoidAlgebra.mem_supported']
  simp [eq_comm]

end CommRing

end Polynomial

namespace AddSubgroup

section CommRing

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (V : AddSubgroup R) [Fintype V]

/-- The *additive polynomial* `∏_{c ∈ V} (X - c)` of a finite additive subgroup `V`: the monic
polynomial whose roots are the elements of `V`, each with multiplicity one. It is Lagrange's
`nodal` polynomial at the nodes `V`. -/
noncomputable def additivePolynomial : R[X] :=
  Lagrange.nodal (Finset.univ : Finset V) (↑)

theorem additivePolynomial_eq_prod : V.additivePolynomial = ∏ c : V, (X - C (c : R)) :=
  Lagrange.nodal_eq _ _

theorem monic_additivePolynomial : V.additivePolynomial.Monic :=
  Lagrange.nodal_monic

@[simp]
theorem natDegree_additivePolynomial [Nontrivial R] :
    V.additivePolynomial.natDegree = Fintype.card V := by
  rw [additivePolynomial, Lagrange.natDegree_nodal, Finset.card_univ]

@[simp]
theorem degree_additivePolynomial [Nontrivial R] :
    V.additivePolynomial.degree = Fintype.card V := by
  rw [additivePolynomial, Lagrange.degree_nodal, Finset.card_univ]

theorem monic_additivePolynomial_sub_C (u : R) :
    (V.additivePolynomial - C u).Monic := by
  nontriviality R using Polynomial.monic_of_subsingleton _
  refine V.monic_additivePolynomial.sub_of_left (degree_C_le.trans_lt ?_)
  rw [degree_additivePolynomial]
  exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos

theorem natDegree_additivePolynomial_sub_C [Nontrivial R] (u : R) :
    (V.additivePolynomial - C u).natDegree = Fintype.card V := by
  rw [natDegree_sub_C, natDegree_additivePolynomial]

/-- A root of `a_V - u` is integral over the base ring. -/
theorem isIntegral_of_aeval_additivePolynomial_eq {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    {u : R} {y : A}
    (hy : aeval y V.additivePolynomial = algebraMap R A u) : IsIntegral R y :=
  ⟨_, V.monic_additivePolynomial_sub_C u, by rw [← aeval_def, map_sub, hy, aeval_C, sub_self]⟩

section Algebra

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]

theorem aeval_additivePolynomial (x : A) :
    aeval x V.additivePolynomial = ∏ c : V, (x - algebraMap R A c) := by
  simp [additivePolynomial_eq_prod]

end Algebra

section Semiring

variable {A : Type*} [Semiring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- Translation by an element of `V` permutes the factors of `a_V`. -/
theorem aeval_additivePolynomial_add_algebraMap (x : A) {c : R} (hc : c ∈ V) :
    aeval (x + algebraMap R A c) V.additivePolynomial = aeval x V.additivePolynomial := by
  -- The universal case `a_V (X + c) = a_V` in `R[X]`, evaluated at `x` below.
  have h : aeval (X + C c) V.additivePolynomial = V.additivePolynomial := by
    rw [aeval_additivePolynomial, additivePolynomial_eq_prod]
    exact Fintype.prod_equiv (Equiv.subRight ⟨c, hc⟩) _ _ fun d ↦ by
      rw [Equiv.subRight_apply, coe_sub, algebraMap_eq, C_sub]; ring
  conv_rhs => rw [← h, ← aeval_algHom_apply, map_add, aeval_X, aeval_C]

@[simp]
theorem aeval_additivePolynomial_algebraMap {c : R} (hc : c ∈ V) :
    aeval (algebraMap R A c) V.additivePolynomial = 0 := by
  rw [aeval_algebraMap_apply_eq_algebraMap_eval, additivePolynomial,
    Lagrange.eval_nodal_at_node (v := ((↑) : V → R)) (Finset.mem_univ ⟨c, hc⟩), map_zero]

/-- The roots of `a_V` in an `R`-algebra `A` without zero divisors, such as a domain or a division
ring, are exactly the images under `algebraMap R A` of the elements of `V`. -/
theorem aeval_additivePolynomial_eq_zero_iff [NoZeroDivisors A] {x : A} :
    aeval x V.additivePolynomial = 0 ↔ ∃ c ∈ V, algebraMap R A c = x := by
  refine ⟨fun hx ↦ ?_, fun ⟨c, hc, hcx⟩ ↦ hcx ▸ V.aeval_additivePolynomial_algebraMap hc⟩
  -- In the zero ring `x = algebraMap R A 0`.
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial A with _ | _
  · exact ⟨0, V.zero_mem, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  -- `aeval x` maps the product of the factors `X - c` to the list product of their values,
  -- so one value vanishes.
  rw [additivePolynomial_eq_prod, ← Finset.prod_map_toList] at hx
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c : V, aeval x (X - C (c : R)) = 0 := by
    simpa [map_list_prod, List.mem_map] using hx
  -- Evaluating `X = (X - c) + c` at `x` gives `x = 0 + c`.
  have hcx := (map_add (aeval x) (X - C (c : R)) (C (c : R))).symm
  simp only [hc, zero_add, aeval_C, sub_add_cancel, aeval_X] at hcx
  exact ⟨c, c.property, hcx⟩

end Semiring

end CommRing

section IsDomain

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] (V : AddSubgroup R) [Fintype V]
variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]

/-- **Additivity of `a_V`.** For a finite additive subgroup `V` of a domain `R`, evaluation of
`a_V` in any commutative `R`-algebra is additive: `a_V (x + y) = a_V x + a_V y`. -/
@[simp]
theorem aeval_additivePolynomial_add (x y : A) :
    aeval (x + y) V.additivePolynomial =
      aeval x V.additivePolynomial + aeval y V.additivePolynomial := by
  -- In a domain, the degree bound and the values on `V` force the difference to vanish.
  have hadd (s t : R[X][X]) :
      aeval (s + t) V.additivePolynomial =
        aeval s V.additivePolynomial + aeval t V.additivePolynomial := by
    set f := V.additivePolynomial.map (algebraMap R R[X][X])
    have hf : f.degree = Fintype.card V := by
      rw [V.monic_additivePolynomial.degree_map, degree_additivePolynomial]
    have hf0 : f ≠ 0 := (V.monic_additivePolynomial.map _).ne_zero
    -- The equal leading terms of `taylor t f` and `f` cancel.
    have hlt : (taylor t f - f - C (aeval t V.additivePolynomial)).degree <
        (Finset.univ : Finset V).card := by
      rw [Finset.card_univ, ← hf]
      refine lt_of_le_of_lt (degree_sub_le _ _) (max_lt ?_ (degree_C_le.trans_lt ?_))
      · rw [← degree_taylor f t]
        exact degree_sub_lt_left (degree_taylor f t) ((taylor_eq_zero t f).not.mpr hf0)
          (leadingCoeff_taylor t f)
      · rw [hf]
        exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
    have hzero := eq_zero_of_degree_lt_of_eval_index_eq_zero (s := Finset.univ)
      (v := fun c : V ↦ algebraMap R R[X][X] c)
      ((FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective R R[X][X]).comp Subtype.val_injective).injOn hlt
      fun c _ ↦ by
        simp only [eval_sub, taylor_eval, eval_C, f, eval_map_algebraMap]
        rw [add_comm, aeval_additivePolynomial_add_algebraMap _ _ c.property,
          aeval_additivePolynomial_algebraMap _ c.property, sub_zero, sub_self]
    have := congrArg (eval s) hzero
    simp only [eval_sub, taylor_eval, eval_C, f, eval_map_algebraMap, eval_zero] at this
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← sub_sub, this]
  -- Evaluate the universal identity at the two elements of the commutative algebra.
  let φ : R[X][X] →ₐ[R] A := aevalTower (aeval y) x
  have h := congrArg φ (hadd (X : R[X][X]) (C X))
  simpa only [map_add, ← aeval_algHom_apply, φ, aevalTower_X, aevalTower_C, aeval_X] using h

@[simp]
theorem aeval_additivePolynomial_sub (x y : A) :
    aeval (x - y) V.additivePolynomial =
      aeval x V.additivePolynomial - aeval y V.additivePolynomial := by
  rw [eq_sub_iff_add_eq, ← aeval_additivePolynomial_add, sub_add_cancel]

/-- If `y` is a root of `a_V - u`, then `a_V - u` is the product of `X - (y + c)` over `c ∈ V`. -/
theorem map_additivePolynomial_sub_C_eq_prod {u : R} {y : A}
    (hy : aeval y V.additivePolynomial = algebraMap R A u) :
    (V.additivePolynomial - C u).map (algebraMap R A) =
      ∏ c : V, (X - C (y + algebraMap R A c)) := by
  have hX : aeval (X : A[X]) V.additivePolynomial = V.additivePolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) := by
    rw [← aeval_map_algebraMap A, aeval_X_left_apply]
  have h := V.aeval_additivePolynomial_sub (A := A[X]) X (C y)
  rw [hX, ← algebraMap_eq (R := A), aeval_algebraMap_apply, hy, algebraMap_eq,
    aeval_additivePolynomial] at h
  rw [Polynomial.map_sub, map_C, ← h]
  refine Fintype.prod_congr _ _ fun c ↦ ?_
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R A A[X], algebraMap_eq, C_add]
  ring

/-- `a_V - u` splits in any commutative `R`-algebra containing one of its roots. -/
theorem splits_additivePolynomial_sub_C {u : R} {y : A}
    (hy : aeval y V.additivePolynomial = algebraMap R A u) :
    ((V.additivePolynomial - C u).map (algebraMap R A)).Splits := by
  rw [V.map_additivePolynomial_sub_C_eq_prod hy]
  exact Splits.prod fun c _ ↦ Splits.X_sub_C _

/-- **The derivative of `a_V` is constant**: `a_V' = ∏_{c ∈ V, c ≠ 0} (-c)`. Over a field this
constant is nonzero, hence a unit, which makes `a_V - u` separable for every `u`. -/
@[simp]
theorem derivative_additivePolynomial :
    derivative V.additivePolynomial = C (∏ᶠ c : {c : V // c ≠ 0}, -(c : R)) := by
  classical
  rw [finprod_eq_prod_of_fintype,
    ← Finset.prod_subtype ((Finset.univ : Finset V).erase 0) (by simp) fun c : V ↦ -(c : R)]
  -- Both sides have degree less than `|V|`, so it suffices to compare them on `V`. At a node `c`
  -- the derivative of the nodal polynomial is `∏_{d ≠ c} (c - d)`, and `d ↦ d - c` reindexes this
  -- product as `∏_{e ≠ 0} (-e)`.
  refine Polynomial.eq_of_degree_sub_lt_of_eval_index_eq (s := Finset.univ) (v := ((↑) : V → R))
    Subtype.val_injective.injOn ?_ fun c _ ↦ ?_
  · rw [Finset.card_univ]
    refine (degree_sub_le _ _).trans_lt (max_lt ?_ (degree_C_le.trans_lt ?_))
    · rw [← V.degree_additivePolynomial]
      exact degree_derivative_lt V.monic_additivePolynomial.ne_zero
    · exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos
  · rw [eval_C, additivePolynomial,
      Lagrange.eval_nodal_derivative_eval_node_eq (Finset.mem_univ c), Lagrange.eval_nodal]
    exact Finset.prod_nbij' (fun d ↦ d - c) (fun e ↦ e + c) (by simp [sub_eq_zero]) (by simp)
      (by simp) (by simp) (by simp)

end IsDomain

section Field

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] (V : AddSubgroup K) [Fintype V]

/-- `a_V - u` is separable. -/
theorem separable_additivePolynomial_sub_C (u : K) : (V.additivePolynomial - C u).Separable := by
  rw [separable_def, derivative_sub, derivative_C, sub_zero, V.derivative_additivePolynomial]
  have hc : (∏ᶠ c : {c : V // c ≠ 0}, -(c : K)) ≠ 0 :=
    finprod_ne_zero fun c ↦ by simpa using c.property
  exact ⟨0, C (∏ᶠ c : {c : V // c ≠ 0}, -(c : K))⁻¹, by simp [← C_mul, hc]⟩

/-- `a_V` is separable: its roots, the elements of `V`, are distinct. -/
theorem separable_additivePolynomial : V.additivePolynomial.Separable := by
  simpa using V.separable_additivePolynomial_sub_C 0

end Field

end AddSubgroup
